{"v":2,"id":"01M7S0S2R142AFEZ9J359XX4KB","ts":"2026-11-19T04:24:30.721604Z","actor":"owner","type":"goal.add","node":"01M7S0S2R142AFEZ9J359XX4KB","payload":{"role":"owner","words":"The communication channel: the owner knows what the agent read, and that what it read reflects hyp's state machine correctly.","base":"c286fa7ad1f6ad6e091647153d8834bc1e984c31","base_tree":"1ea60e1e61c83fbdb77d7a2d70b3901bed31ee39","budget":3,"from":"","lines":[{"key":"line-1","text":"The communication channel, which is used for `hyp` to communicate with agent, is one block of code, defined with Go as code that has a boundary, such as one Go module, one object or one state machine.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-2","text":"The owner can read exactly what the agent read.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-3","text":"hyp tells the owner and the agent something its state doesn't hold.","kind":"gap"}]},"why":"Rerun of G-NXHHVA (#183) under v2"}
{"v":2,"id":"01M7SET8YCPJN388JPD73FDQC0","ts":"2026-11-19T08:29:49.900597Z","actor":"owner","type":"goal.add","node":"01M7SET8YCPJN388JPD73FDQC0","payload":{"role":"owner","words":"Take reads back out of the log","base":"ecc023fcb45da2a506a375ae48c45a43ba7099dd","base_tree":"8548a3f5ad9b380cac2c42e74036251969e025b4","budget":3,"from":"","lines":[{"key":"line-1","text":"When multiple agents, or owner read when running `hyp status`, the line was added, which make unintended code changes","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-2","text":"The owner can read exactly what the agent read.","kind":"guard"}]},"why":"Reads leave a trace (#226) put each read into tracked files; separate the trace from the log, keep hyp show"}
{"v":2,"id":"01M7SJRNX7SA2Y6MDWGXRK4VYD","ts":"2026-11-19T09:38:51.943277Z","actor":"owner","type":"goal.add","node":"01M7SJRNX7SA2Y6MDWGXRK4VYD","payload":{"role":"owner","words":"Keep the trace in hyp's own folder, and let the owner clean it","base":"a4e751ee50642eceb4bddbef329f1bccd4d02992","base_tree":"caec7bf2efd1acd5db269106541128b44c02ed76","budget":3,"from":"01M7SET8YCPJN388JPD73FDQC0","lines":[{"key":"line-1","text":"hyp keeps the trace under ~/.hyp/trace or something similar, and does not hijack the ~/.local folder.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-2","text":"The owner can see and remove the traces of repositories that no longer exist.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-3","text":"The owner can read an agent's reads from any git worktree of the clone the agent used, before its branch merges.","kind":"guard"}]},"why":""}
{"v":2,"id":"01M7T5ESTMKJNEYXGRAV1908D1","ts":"2026-11-19T15:05:31.220853Z","actor":"owner","type":"goal.add","node":"01M7T5ESTMKJNEYXGRAV1908D1","payload":{"role":"owner","words":"While a line has no example, status offers a further example on a line that has one","base":"96f9406f8f5a7f51aa7228c2699a87aef426b9c2","base_tree":"35ddbf3aebbf91a0052dbeea9b79242efb066bc0","budget":3,"from":"","lines":[{"key":"line-1","text":"The grill's allowed acts list every place that the guards allow, including a further example on a line that already holds one, as ready command lines.","kind":"gap"}]},"why":""}
{"v":2,"id":"01M7T4XZHP1Z198DWGCQCJWT9T","ts":"2026-11-19T14:56:20.022985Z","actor":"owner","type":"goal.add","node":"01M7T4XZHP1Z198DWGCQCJWT9T","payload":{"role":"owner","words":"See a verdict before it is recorded","base":"96f9406f8f5a7f51aa7228c2699a87aef426b9c2","base_tree":"35ddbf3aebbf91a0052dbeea9b79242efb066bc0","budget":3,"from":"","lines":[{"key":"line-1","text":"An agent can see an example's output, stderr, exit code and verdict, as hyp would record them, on H0 or on an uncommitted change, without a commit, without recording anything in the log, and without using a Hypothesis.","kind":"gap"}]},"why":""}
{"v":2,"id":"01M7VEV2AR2JX2WGB1HEH7GGGK","ts":"2026-11-20T03:08:44.760813Z","actor":"owner","type":"goal.add","node":"01M7VEV2AR2JX2WGB1HEH7GGGK","payload":{"role":"owner","words":"A grill skill that ships with hyp","base":"f93b747a96535ffd67b04bafebd74b4042918bdb","base_tree":"ced92f9058cfb6a91720b2bc0babc9866e053d37","budget":3,"from":"","lines":[{"key":"line-1","text":"A user of hyp in another repository can grill and re-grill a Goal with no prompt written by hand.","kind":"gap"}]},"why":"Issue #248"}
{"v":2,"id":"01M7W3QCGF5E1XP0YMK1M66KKY","ts":"2026-11-20T09:13:44.207601Z","actor":"owner","type":"goal.add","node":"01M7W3QCGF5E1XP0YMK1M66KKY","payload":{"role":"owner","words":"A Goal's stop and its land are two events: a stop ends the runs, and the owner's land ends the Goal as a fixed snapshot that later Goals build on.","base":"f73546b441784c6c52621424bed10bab2ddadd27","base_tree":"05038aa1f88f3776a98e474e7ebdcda686d0b536","budget":3,"from":"","lines":[{"key":"line-1","text":"After a Goal reaches a stop, the owner lands it with one act that hyp status prints. The act records one land event in the log, which names the stop it ends, whether or not the change was merged. A land by another role, or on a Goal with no stop, is refused.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-2","text":"hyp status shows a stop as an event: which stop, the act that caused it, and when.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-3","text":"A landed Goal prints the record of its decision, the PR body or with no select the table of outputs, in hyp status G and in the land act's return; hyp status for every Goal prints only its state block.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-4","text":"After a select, hyp status shows the Goal waiting for the owner, and prints the land line among the owner's acts.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-5","text":"A landed Goal is fixed: hyp refuses place, run, select and a second land on it.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-6","text":"hyp add goal --from G is refused unless G is landed.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-7","text":"The glossary and the spec describe land as the owner's event that ends a Goal, not as a check of a commit, and say what the snapshot is, when it is read and what for.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-8","text":"A selected Goal that is not landed still refuses place, run and a second select.","kind":"guard"},{"key":"line-9","text":"A log written before land existed, in which a Goal cites a Goal that is not landed, replays with nothing refused.","kind":"guard"}]},"why":"#245"}
{"v":2,"id":"01M7W6K9RV33NZC2XKYNJ12TX3","ts":"2026-11-20T10:03:56.059819Z","actor":"owner","type":"land","node":"01M7W3QCGF5E1XP0YMK1M66KKY","payload":{"role":"owner","stop":"selected","cause":"01M7W5XB38W6M3E1Q8WWEKN4ZF"},"why":"#245"}
{"v":2,"id":"01M7W7ZGNT13KS2YHNEQG2R3VG","ts":"2026-11-20T10:28:04.922698Z","actor":"owner","type":"goal.add","node":"01M7W7ZGNT13KS2YHNEQG2R3VG","payload":{"role":"owner","words":"The grill writes a Goal's model with what hyp ships, every rule the model checks has a switch, and the owner reads its chart in the select report.","base":"24b759e20b85e5113779bbe5bc535742874663c9","base_tree":"9e8fb6876e87761b97d67efd9812d4db79a28f5b","budget":3,"from":"","lines":[{"key":"line-1","text":"When a commit's spec holds a model, select refuses it if a rule the model checks is named by no switch config, or if it holds no chart, and the refusal names each such rule or the missing chart.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-2","text":"The select report shows the Goal's chart, so the owner reads it in the PR without the runner pasting it.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-3","text":"A user of hyp in another repository can have the grill write a Goal's model, with one switch per cheap wrong build, each tried as a patch with hyp try --worktree, and its chart, with what hyp ships and the tools it names and no prompt written by hand.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-4","text":"A commit whose spec folder holds no model is selected as before.","kind":"guard"}]},"why":"#247: the owner's decisions of 2026-11-20"}
{"v":2,"id":"01M7W9X90RN7FEX8G6S7RXBGRG","ts":"2026-11-20T11:01:48.696741Z","actor":"owner","type":"land","node":"01M7W7ZGNT13KS2YHNEQG2R3VG","payload":{"role":"owner","stop":"selected","cause":"01M7W9QAXHZ71EBM7H6WCMA4Q7"},"why":"Every line met on row 9a1e2fb; owner merged PR #265"}
{"v":2,"id":"01M7WBED30WTW30X4DM3VDG87A","ts":"2026-11-20T11:28:38.496541Z","actor":"owner","type":"goal.add","node":"01M7WBED30WTW30X4DM3VDG87A","payload":{"role":"owner","words":"The owner can put a selected Goal back to open with unselect, so a re-grill or a recheck after main moves happens inside the same Goal.","base":"9d267f755f2894f68a1b3e4224684b1d92c67742","base_tree":"5249bf7979d32fd0fb016068f46e79e5afb9a412","budget":3,"from":"","lines":[{"key":"line-1","text":"After the owner unselects a selected Goal, the Goal is open again: the grill may place, the runner may run, and a new select is recorded.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-2","text":"After an unselect the budget starts again at 0 of 3, and H0's row and the old candidate's row keep their live cells.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-3","text":"unselect is refused, exit 1, on a landed Goal, on a Goal that is not selected, and by any actor or role but the owner who added the Goal.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-4","text":"After an unselect, a runner's select is refused until a run records a cell for an example version or a row that was not run before the unselect; a rerun of the same example version on the same row does not count. The owner may select at any time.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-5","text":"A Goal that was never unselected keeps the state, stop and allowed acts it has today.","kind":"guard"}]},"why":"#246"}
{"v":2,"id":"01M7WJSTFC9FX8WGA0CRM50H4M","ts":"2026-11-20T13:37:12.684825Z","actor":"owner","type":"land","node":"01M7WBED30WTW30X4DM3VDG87A","payload":{"role":"owner","stop":"selected","cause":"01M7WJH0MA35KYQ0MGFAV9ZKM0"},"why":""}
{"v":2,"id":"01M7YKQHSVRKBXTTQ6KNSCAXYW","ts":"2026-11-21T08:31:55.707542Z","actor":"owner","type":"goal.add","node":"01M7YKQHSVRKBXTTQ6KNSCAXYW","payload":{"role":"owner","words":"The statechart tool, not the grill, says which rules each variant breaks and which examples each variant would meet; the grill tries what the tool predicts, and only a tried variant that meets every example reaches the owner, as one plain question.","base":"a26b5c996d8b197eb04c2f722db235777828dc99","base_tree":"4c65b1b0ed70d36f831e102b4d9e3b8dbbf93264","budget":3,"from":"","lines":[{"key":"line-1","text":"The statechart tool writes one variant config per variant that lists exactly the rules that variant breaks, and prints each rule that no variant breaks as not shown to fail.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-2","text":"For each example of a Goal, the tool prints a walk of the model whose last state prints what meets the example's floors and ceilings, or says that no walk of the model does.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-3","text":"For each example and each variant, the tool prints whether the example is met under that variant, from the model alone and with no patch, and for each variant it prints the examples that separate it, or none.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-4","text":"The report holds a rules table (rule, source, broken by, an example sees it break), an examples by variants table with predicted and tried cells and a separated-by row, and one part for each variant that no example separates, naming its rules, the step no example takes and the two prints; when the grill gives the tool the verdicts `hyp try --worktree` printed on a variant's patch, each tried cell sits beside its prediction and each cell where they differ is named.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-5","text":"Each rule of the model names its source: a line of the Goal, an owner decision, or model only. The tool lists each rule with no source and each line of the Goal that no rule names.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-6","text":"A user of hyp in another repository can have the grill draft the model after the owner consents to the words and lines and before the examples are final, try with `hyp try --worktree` each variant the tool predicts to meet every example and one predicted-fail example of each other variant, and fix the model, not an example, where a try differs from its prediction, saying so in one line of the hand-off.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-7","text":"A user of hyp in another repository gets from the grill one plain-English question, at the example level and with no model word, for each tried variant that meets every example and prints something else on a step no example takes; a case the owner answers \"either output is fine\" goes under Not covered.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-8","text":"hyp, the glossary, the spec and both skills say \"variant\" where they said \"switch\": select reads variant configs from `specs/variants/`, and its refusal names variant configs.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-9","text":"A commit whose spec folder holds its variant configs under `specs/switches/` is selected or refused as before.","kind":"guard"},{"key":"line-10","text":"A commit whose spec folder holds no model is selected as before, and hyp runs no model checker and reads no model report.","kind":"guard"}]},"why":"Issue #283: the grill writes switch configs by hand, and they name rules their switch does not break (G-1908D1, #243, #247, #272, #235)."}
{"v":2,"id":"01M7YKZSAR6HDJSCAFAGG0SSP5","ts":"2026-11-21T08:36:25.560151Z","actor":"owner","type":"goal.add","node":"01M7YKQHSVRKBXTTQ6KNSCAXYW","payload":{"role":"owner","words":"The statechart tool, not the grill, says which rules each variant breaks and which examples each variant would meet; the grill tries what the tool predicts, and only a tried variant that meets every example reaches the owner, as one plain question.","base":"a26b5c996d8b197eb04c2f722db235777828dc99","base_tree":"4c65b1b0ed70d36f831e102b4d9e3b8dbbf93264","budget":3,"from":"","lines":[{"key":"line-1","text":"The statechart tool writes one variant config per variant that lists exactly the rules that variant breaks, and prints each rule that no variant breaks as not shown to fail.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-2","text":"For each example of a Goal, the tool prints a walk of the model along which the model's prints give an output that meets the example's floors and ceilings, or says that no walk of the model does.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-3","text":"For each example and each variant, the tool prints whether the example is met under that variant, from the model alone and with no patch, and for each variant it prints the examples that separate it, or none.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-4","text":"The report holds a rules table (rule, source, broken by, an example sees it break), an examples by variants table with predicted and tried cells and a separated-by row, and one part for each variant that no example separates, naming its rules, the step no example takes and the two prints; when the grill gives the tool the verdicts `hyp try --worktree` printed on a variant's patch, each tried cell sits beside its prediction and each cell where they differ is named.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-5","text":"Each rule of the model names its source: a line of the Goal, an owner decision, or model only. The tool lists each rule with no source and each line of the Goal that no rule names.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-6","text":"A user of hyp in another repository can have the grill draft the model after the owner consents to the words and lines and before the examples are final, try with `hyp try --worktree` each variant the tool predicts to meet every example and one predicted-fail example of each other variant, and fix the model, not an example, where a try differs from its prediction, saying so in one line of the hand-off.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-7","text":"A user of hyp in another repository gets from the grill one plain-English question, at the example level and with no model word, for each tried variant that meets every example and prints something else on a step no example takes; a case the owner answers \"either output is fine\" goes under Not covered.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-8","text":"hyp, the glossary, the spec and both skills say \"variant\" where they said \"switch\": select reads variant configs from `specs/variants/`, and its refusal names variant configs.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-9","text":"A commit whose spec folder holds its variant configs under `specs/switches/` is selected or refused as before.","kind":"guard"},{"key":"line-10","text":"A commit whose spec folder holds no model is selected as before, and hyp runs no model checker and reads no model report.","kind":"guard"}]},"why":"Replace: line-2 matched only the last state, but a floor holds prints along a walk. Issue #283: the grill writes switch configs by hand, and they name rules their switch does not break (G-1908D1, #243, #247, #272, #235)."}
{"v":2,"id":"01M7YQM8K9Z78M4KB3R5HRCPHB","ts":"2026-11-21T09:40:02.281419Z","actor":"owner","type":"land","node":"01M7YKQHSVRKBXTTQ6KNSCAXYW","payload":{"role":"owner","stop":"selected","cause":"01M7YPQZMGKMQ609F2Q4T689MC"},"why":""}
{"v":2,"id":"01M7YR83ETYV4Y01TZQEX0HY3A","ts":"2026-11-21T09:50:52.378534Z","actor":"owner","type":"goal.add","node":"01M7YR83ETYV4Y01TZQEX0HY3A","payload":{"role":"owner","words":"Every agent reads from hyp what a written or open Goal asks, and the grill reads what a cited Goal decided, so no agent reads a Goal from the store by hand.","base":"4882df16421741d4638672ed51180f9197c5d0a4","base_tree":"42b364c73ea80ea37b53cc42e084884444ff82cc","budget":3,"from":"","lines":[{"key":"line-1","text":"While a Goal is written or open, `hyp status G`, with or without `--role`, prints the Goal's words, each line's key and text, and for each placed example its key, words, run, floors, ceilings and its verdict on H0 at place.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-2","text":"`hyp status` for every Goal, the return of every act that writes, and `hyp status G` of a selected or landed Goal print what they print on H0.","kind":"guard"},{"key":"line-3","text":"When the Goal the grill drafts will cite a landed Goal with `--from`, the grill skill tells the grill to read `hyp status` of that Goal before it drafts the words and lines.","kind":"gap"}]},"why":"#287, with #258 as a line; owner decisions in https://github.com/dat9uy/hyp/issues/287#issuecomment-7060830160"}
