{"v":2,"id":"01M7YSVGHD8YY8JGN81XTN85JM","ts":"2026-11-21T10:18:56.941279Z","actor":"owner","type":"land","node":"01M7YR83ETYV4Y01TZQEX0HY3A","payload":{"role":"owner","stop":"selected","cause":"01M7YSM3516271QZQY2CJ7AZ0X"},"why":"the selected change merged in #293"}
{"v":2,"id":"01M7YV78CA4DJV3F5K8RHKKGFK","ts":"2026-11-21T10:42:50.378593Z","actor":"owner","type":"goal.add","node":"01M7YV78CA4DJV3F5K8RHKKGFK","payload":{"role":"owner","words":"The grill stops trying a variant at its first failed example, and the statechart report counts that failed try as separating the variant.","base":"c7429ea86ff68697181c6c093f2c31a0c70af971","base_tree":"58040898eb22653d25e7f48f8899ee4df9cb92fd","budget":3,"from":"01M7YKQHSVRKBXTTQ6KNSCAXYW","lines":[{"key":"line-1","text":"For each variant, the statechart report counts an example as separating it when the example's tried verdict on the variant's patch is a fail, or when the example was not tried and the tool predicts it to fail; a tried met stands over a predicted fail.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-2","text":"The hyp-grill and hyp-statechart skills tell the grill to stop trying a variant at its first failed example, and to try first the example the tool predicts the variant to fail, or, with no prediction, the examples on the source lines of the rules it breaks; no skill file keeps a rule to try a predicted-fail example once more as a spot check.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-3","text":"A variant whose every tried verdict is met, and on which the tool predicts no untried example to fail, is still reported as separated by none, with its part naming the rules it breaks.","kind":"guard"}]},"why":"#289: owner decision 1, \"Stop at first fail (Recommended)\""}
{"v":2,"id":"01M7YWDDXNG41EPJSJJZNPQPY0","ts":"2026-11-21T11:03:41.237789Z","actor":"owner","type":"land","node":"01M7YV78CA4DJV3F5K8RHKKGFK","payload":{"role":"owner","stop":"selected","cause":"01M7YWAAFAE5BAV218QJXHNZ6C"},"why":"#289: selected change merged in #296"}
{"v":2,"id":"01M7YXC0V5B5AATK3YPFGRXA9K","ts":"2026-11-21T11:20:23.653444Z","actor":"owner","type":"goal.add","node":"01M7YXC0V5B5AATK3YPFGRXA9K","payload":{"role":"owner","words":"hyp prints the Probe writer's contract, so an agent asked to write an example's Probe follows one stated rule instead of guessing.","base":"6bcab496d7b4c4d243cc055b9b5d2666f62cac82","base_tree":"dbae43df6fd71ccbf702a0240c7b862e45116ca2","budget":3,"from":"","lines":[{"key":"line-1","text":"While a Goal is written or open, hyp status G and hyp status G --role probe-writer print in the probe-writer block the Probe writer's contract, the generic Probe, and one task for each line of the Goal. The contract says: read the line, its example and H0; write and commit only that example's probe folder; start from the generic Probe and write new code only when it cannot run the example; run the example on H0 with hyp try and return its output; write no event.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-2","text":"What hyp status prints for the owner, the grill and the runner, what hyp status with no Goal prints, and the probe-writer block of a selected or landed Goal stay as they are.","kind":"guard"}]},"why":"Issue #279: no skill or doc states the Probe writer's contract. Owner decisions are on #279."}
{"v":2,"id":"01M7Z38YEKTTACTWF89E00FV3X","ts":"2026-11-21T13:03:34.355944Z","actor":"owner","type":"land","node":"01M7YXC0V5B5AATK3YPFGRXA9K","payload":{"role":"owner","stop":"selected","cause":"01M7Z1JKJTSZKA3M3FRTH2H1N8"},"why":""}
{"v":2,"id":"01M7Z44YVRC6MTX5E8CDD2MVSR","ts":"2026-11-21T13:18:52.280137Z","actor":"owner","type":"goal.add","node":"01M7Z44YVRC6MTX5E8CDD2MVSR","payload":{"role":"owner","words":"A grill that follows the hyp-grill skill makes the moves the owner agreed for v2: in the first grill, in the re-grill, and when it tries variants and hands an example to the Probe writer.","base":"9e0b632b186e3ba2bfdb831a5bbe8f4c321f8875","base_tree":"0f953acf01280c17e1b23e8813612853fbc10c7f","budget":3,"from":"01M7YXC0V5B5AATK3YPFGRXA9K","lines":[{"key":"line-1","text":"In a first grill of a written Goal's examples, the grill asks for each line \"What would you do, and what would you see?\" and makes the owner's answer that line's example, without reading it back for approval; when an answer has two things to see, it warns that the line combines two rules and proposes a split, which the owner decides; it writes the floor from the want, reads the line's \"must never\" words aloud and asks \"What could a wrong build print that this floor still lets through?\", and each wrong output the owner names becomes a ceiling; and once every line has an example that gives its line's verdict on H0, it stops asking and says the Goal has enough.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-2","text":"In a re-grill at a stop, when the owner reports something odd, the grill asks the owner to state it as \"on input X, I must see Y\" or \"I must never see Y\", and proposes an adjust when a line's words already ask for Y or forbid it, and a new Goal when Y needs new words.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-3","text":"When the grill tries a Goal's variants, it stops trying a variant at its first failed example. When the generic Probe cannot run an example, the grill hands that example to a Probe writer that it starts with what hyp status G prints for the Probe writer, and writes no new Probe code itself; an example the generic Probe can run gets the generic Probe.","kind":"gap"}]},"why":"Issue #279: the grill moves agreed for v2 are in no skill. Owner decisions are on #279."}
{"v":2,"id":"01M7Z7R62NNS220C6XTM1S8W9P","ts":"2026-11-21T14:21:47.989625Z","actor":"owner","type":"land","node":"01M7Z44YVRC6MTX5E8CDD2MVSR","payload":{"role":"owner","stop":"selected","cause":"01M7Z6GTVDXBDF4R37W32G24SR"},"why":"Owner, 2026-11-21: \"let land the goal in the same PR\" (PR #303). Selected on H1, merged in #301."}
{"v":2,"id":"01M81KPS51SDFP40THK4SBFXAY","ts":"2026-11-22T12:29:13.761197Z","actor":"owner","type":"goal.add","node":"01M81KPS51SDFP40THK4SBFXAY","payload":{"role":"owner","words":"The grill places a Goal's whole example set with one `hyp place G`, and the set counts only when every example agrees with its line about H0.","base":"b80bf19b78734b3bdaaf2cf7ba99be955a72edd0","base_tree":"4cd1c2d50221c1b28691b209c6e7bdf5c86af29d","budget":3,"from":"01M7T5ESTMKJNEYXGRAV1908D1","lines":[{"key":"line-1","text":"`hyp place G` places every example under `goals/G/\u003cline\u003e/` in one act, and only when each example agrees with its line about H0: a gap example fails on H0, a guard example is met on H0.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-2","text":"When an example disagrees with its line about H0, `hyp place G` places none of the set and names each example that disagrees, in its line's words.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-3","text":"`hyp place G` places none of the set, and names each cause, when a line holds no example, when an example placed before is missing, when an example is not committed, or when a new version changes more than its floors and ceilings.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-4","text":"A `hyp place G` that changes no example is refused, and only a place that changed the set restarts the budget; a change under `goals/G/specs/` alone is no change.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-5","text":"While the Goal is written or open, the grill's allowed acts show one ready place line, `hyp place G`; the form `hyp place G LINE/EXAMPLE` is refused as a bad argument.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-6","text":"Every Goal recorded before this change keeps the state, stop, runs and allowed acts `hyp status` prints for it.","kind":"guard"}]},"why":"issue #312"}
{"v":2,"id":"01M81QFAZC03Z8TCW4MBRYSZH0","ts":"2026-11-22T13:35:04.172701Z","actor":"owner","type":"land","node":"01M81KPS51SDFP40THK4SBFXAY","payload":{"role":"owner","stop":"selected","cause":"01M81Q9CSA7SZA67ZA0WMA7F6A"},"why":""}
{"v":2,"id":"01M81T827VTYRMW7D0XNG4NNT7","ts":"2026-11-22T14:23:31.579231Z","actor":"owner","type":"goal.add","node":"01M81T827VTYRMW7D0XNG4NNT7","payload":{"role":"owner","words":"Git keeps only the owner's acts, the place of each example set and the select, while every cell, Result and output stays in the clone's trace as a cache that a reader fills by running an example again, and hyp warns when a selected commit is on no branch or tag.","base":"4c1b0c104df5119bb0e5fbd7e98bc1d6a77ec3b9","base_tree":"d2fa93c54370b073c4959a3fe1a0f9d8bac77428","budget":3,"from":"","lines":[{"key":"line-1","text":"`hyp place G` writes to `.tree/` only one line that names the example set's hashes; H0's cells and outputs go to the clone's trace.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-2","text":"`hyp run` writes nothing under `.tree/`, and `hyp select` writes to `.tree/` only one line that names the commit and the example hashes it was judged by; Results and outputs go to the clone's trace.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-3","text":"In a clone whose trace lacks a cell that `hyp status G` would print, it says the cell is not in this clone's trace and prints the ready `hyp try` line that runs it again.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-4","text":"A `hyp try` of a missing cell saves that cell in the clone's trace, and `hyp status G` then prints it, marked as run again in this clone.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-5","text":"Every state block of a selected or landed Goal (`hyp status`, `hyp status G`, and the return of `hyp select` and `hyp land`) prints a warning when the selected commit is on no branch or tag, also when another commit with the same subject hash is on one.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-6","text":"In a clone whose trace holds no run of an open Goal, `hyp status G` prints `runs: 0 of 3 used`, whatever other clones ran.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-7","text":"`hyp status G` of every landed Goal on main prints as it does on the base.","kind":"guard"},{"key":"line-8","text":"A runner in a fresh clone of the record branch can run every line of an open Goal and select a candidate met on every line.","kind":"guard"}]},"why":"Grilled from #313: git keeps only the owner's acts and the set's place; evidence moves to the trace."}
{"v":2,"id":"01M832VQHWQVPWEB347TGF11ED","ts":"2026-11-23T02:13:19.03699Z","actor":"owner","type":"goal.add","node":"01M832VQHWQVPWEB347TGF11ED","payload":{"role":"owner","words":"The owner ends a Goal with land or close, and an ended Goal holds exactly what it held when the owner ended it, in every clone.","base":"68d7647a8d4527447b43ac171567bef3ccbcb9b0","base_tree":"bc3ad1e67ae7a5abc107da77ff61be34f2e8c086","budget":3,"from":"","lines":[{"key":"line-1","text":"The owner closes a Goal that is not ended with one act hyp status prints, and status then shows it `ended` with a line naming the close, its actor and time; a close by another role or actor is refused.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-2","text":"A landed Goal shows `ended`, with a line naming the land.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-3","text":"After a land or close, a Result or select written in another clone before it that the end does not name is refused at replay and listed under 'refused at replay', so the ended Goal's rows and verdicts are those the owner saw.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-4","text":"A closed Goal refuses place, run, select, unselect, land and a second close.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-5","text":"`hyp add goal --from G` accepts a closed Goal like a landed one.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-6","text":"Land on a Goal whose runs have not stopped is refused.","kind":"guard"},{"key":"line-7","text":"A log written before close existed replays with nothing refused, and each Goal keeps its rows and verdicts.","kind":"guard"}]},"why":"Issue #329: the owner has no act to end a Goal that will not go on, so G-G4NNT7 stays open in main."}
{"v":2,"id":"01M834VPVPJ6ZP552FVGV6VNQB","ts":"2026-11-23T02:48:15.478506Z","actor":"owner","type":"land","node":"01M832VQHWQVPWEB347TGF11ED","payload":{"role":"owner","stop":"selected","cause":"01M834DGXT1FTWD7XMDBNY1RRF"},"why":"selected candidate meets every line"}
{"v":2,"id":"01M8351CP47C2B5FSHW078MW3S","ts":"2026-11-23T02:51:21.668351Z","actor":"owner","type":"close","node":"01M81T827VTYRMW7D0XNG4NNT7","payload":{"role":"owner","seen":["01M81T827VTYRMW7D0XNG4NNT7","01M81VZMMHQ4CJM13EHRCWZE56"]},"why":"PR #324 was closed unmerged; the question goes on as #313, after #328."}
{"v":2,"id":"01M835A3GGPKCKXVHN0SDR449G","ts":"2026-11-23T02:56:07.184631Z","actor":"owner","type":"goal.add","node":"01M835A3GGPKCKXVHN0SDR449G","payload":{"role":"owner","words":"Each event kind, state and act of hyp is one entry that hyp both acts on and prints with `hyp spec`, so changing a rule changes one entry, and the prose docs keep only reasons, words and how to use hyp.","base":"6aa4ae6c78b09437e31352893a9c2b5ff8aee6b5","base_tree":"3ce34fb11e659e2bc073868debcbc06b22a015ea","budget":3,"from":"","lines":[{"key":"line-1","text":"`hyp spec` prints every event kind with where it is stored (git or the clone's trace), the Goal it belongs to, and whether an end freezes it; each act stores its event where `hyp spec` says.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-2","text":"`hyp spec` prints every state with the acts it refuses and the guard that refuses each, and every act with its roles and its guards in order; in each state an act is refused by the guard `hyp spec` names, and `hyp status` offers an act only where `hyp spec` allows it.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-3","text":"`hyp spec` prints every act's usage line and every refusal code with its exit code, and `hyp help` and each refusal agree with it.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-4","text":"`docs/` holds no `state-machine.md`; `owner-guide.md` tells only how to use the skills and the flow hyp-grill, then run, then land, close or re-grill; AGENTS.md and the README name `hyp spec` as the spec.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-5","text":"No doc under `docs/`, ADRs aside, names a Goal or an issue as the source of a rule.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-6","text":"Replaying the git log gives the same states and refusals in every clone, whatever that clone's trace holds.","kind":"guard"},{"key":"line-7","text":"Every output and exit code hyp prints today, other than `hyp help`, is unchanged.","kind":"guard"}]},"why":"Issue #328: one storage rule took 26 Go files and 5 docs (PR #324), one act took 32 files (G-GF11ED), and nothing checks the prose spec against the code."}
{"v":2,"id":"01M837ENRNBQN9M8M497G6SYHA","ts":"2026-11-23T03:33:34.101064Z","actor":"owner","type":"land","node":"01M835A3GGPKCKXVHN0SDR449G","payload":{"role":"owner","stop":"selected","cause":"01M8378CHT9VT6C2YQ4AGJ36TE","seen":["01M835A3GGPKCKXVHN0SDR449G","01M835M3EJ1WNHZ853AF5KGW1Y","01M8377B57316TNE9R76R1G27M","01M8377N3839Q2G5W441Y4QE4H","01M8377QK9J8P9BS4XCCTGNX77","01M8377RM0MWEY71D1RQRSAGDX","01M8377SBH9AEA541QH5CQNM99","01M8377XZ4DW67EJ0HR80NHC2M","01M837812KYDNK898TN5QH9P6D","01M8378CHT9VT6C2YQ4AGJ36TE"]},"why":""}
{"v":2,"id":"01M838XYHFEFB01M5YTNQJABD8","ts":"2026-11-23T03:59:23.183935Z","actor":"owner","type":"goal.add","node":"01M838XYHFEFB01M5YTNQJABD8","payload":{"role":"owner","words":"Git keeps only the events that change a Goal's state, and hyp stores each event kind from that one rule, so every clone replays the same Goal states and refusals from git. Every Result and output stays in the clone's trace as a cache that a reader fills by running an example again, and hyp warns when a selected commit is on no branch or tag.","base":"da86fbbc63122871bb80e2a6249ef52bc205a286","base_tree":"a18a739f85f0bfe1e63f69da32a013f4ef789baa","budget":3,"from":"","lines":[{"key":"line-1","text":"`hyp spec` says for each event kind whether it changes a Goal's state, and each act stores its event in git when it does and in the clone's trace when it does not; `result.record` is stored in the trace.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-2","text":"`hyp spec` says for each guard whether replay checks it, and a guard that replay checks reads only events stored in git.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-3","text":"`hyp place G` writes to `.tree/` only one line that names each example's hash and its verdict on H0, and no file under `.tree/outputs/`; H0's outputs go to the clone's trace.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-4","text":"`hyp run` writes nothing under `.tree/`, and `hyp status` counts runs and the stops `two candidates` and `budget used` only from this clone's trace.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-5","text":"In a clone whose trace lacks a cell that `hyp status G` would print, it says the cell is not in this clone's trace and prints the ready `hyp try` line that runs it again.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-6","text":"A `hyp try` of a missing cell saves that cell in the clone's trace, and `hyp status G` then prints it, marked as run again in this clone.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-7","text":"Every state block of a selected or landed Goal (`hyp status`, `hyp status G`, and the return of `hyp select` and `hyp land`) prints a warning when the selected commit is on no branch or tag, also when another commit with the same subject hash is on one.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-8","text":"In a fresh clone with an empty trace, `hyp status G` of a Goal placed, run and selected in another clone shows the same state as that clone, and lists no event under `refused at replay`.","kind":"guard"},{"key":"line-9","text":"A runner in a fresh clone of the record branch can run every line of an open Goal and select a candidate met on every line.","kind":"guard"},{"key":"line-10","text":"`hyp status G` of every landed Goal on main prints as it does on the base.","kind":"guard"}]},"why":"Goal of #313 after G-DR449G (#335): one rule decides where each event is stored; decisions 1-14 on #313"}
{"v":2,"id":"01M83CE72HDDSKMC10WSF7YMPP","ts":"2026-11-23T05:00:41.937029Z","actor":"owner","type":"close","node":"01M838XYHFEFB01M5YTNQJABD8","payload":{"role":"owner","seen":["01M838XYHFEFB01M5YTNQJABD8","01M839QSCD4TVJ70TH9KZPX7WT"]},"why":"four Probes no build can meet; replaced by a new Goal --from G-QJABD8 (#313, #339)"}
{"v":2,"id":"01M83CHVDCZXR89JSSP69KAEW6","ts":"2026-11-23T05:02:41.068816Z","actor":"owner","type":"goal.add","node":"01M83CHVDCZXR89JSSP69KAEW6","payload":{"role":"owner","words":"Git keeps only the events that change a Goal's state, and hyp stores each event kind from that one rule, so every clone replays the same Goal states and refusals from git. Every Result and output stays in the clone's trace as a cache that a reader fills by running an example again, and hyp warns when a selected commit is on no branch or tag.","base":"e683521e4e2fb92b34c9daebbfcf33727fe3f015","base_tree":"a18a739f85f0bfe1e63f69da32a013f4ef789baa","budget":3,"from":"01M838XYHFEFB01M5YTNQJABD8","lines":[{"key":"line-1","text":"`hyp spec` says for each event kind whether it changes a Goal's state, and each act stores its event in git when it does and in the clone's trace when it does not; `result.record` is stored in the trace, and the outputs a clone keeps are files in its trace, not an event kind: `hyp spec` lists no event kind that the base does not list.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-2","text":"`hyp spec` says for each guard whether replay checks it, and a guard that replay checks reads only events stored in git.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-3","text":"`hyp place G` writes to `.tree/` only one line that names each example's hash and its verdict on H0, and no file under `.tree/outputs/`; H0's outputs go to the clone's trace.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-4","text":"`hyp run` writes nothing under `.tree/`, and `hyp status` counts runs and the stops `two candidates` and `budget used` only from this clone's trace.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-5","text":"In a clone whose trace lacks a cell that `hyp status G` would print, it says the cell is not in this clone's trace and prints the ready `hyp try` line that runs it again.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-6","text":"A `hyp try` of a missing cell saves that cell in the clone's trace, and `hyp status G` then prints it, marked as run again in this clone; when its verdict differs from the verdict git holds, `hyp status G` prints both verdicts and a warning that the example gave two verdicts.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-7","text":"Every state block of a selected or landed Goal (`hyp status`, `hyp status G`, and the return of `hyp select` and `hyp land`) prints a warning when the selected commit is on no branch or tag, also when another commit with the same subject hash is on one.","kind":"gap"},{"key":"line-8","text":"In a fresh clone with an empty trace, `hyp status G` of a Goal placed, run and selected in another clone shows the same state as that clone, and lists no event under `refused at replay`.","kind":"guard"},{"key":"line-9","text":"A runner in a fresh clone of the record branch can run every line of an open Goal and select a candidate met on every line.","kind":"guard"},{"key":"line-10","text":"`hyp status G` of every landed Goal on main prints as it does on the base.","kind":"guard"}]},"why":"replaces G-QJABD8, whose four Probes no build can meet (#313, #339)"}
{"v":2,"id":"01M83GBRZTMNDH6HFCDZWFMRQF","ts":"2026-11-23T06:09:16.282276Z","actor":"owner","type":"land","node":"01M83CHVDCZXR89JSSP69KAEW6","payload":{"role":"owner","stop":"selected","cause":"01M83FX7SX9YW561N14X2ARVFX","seen":["01M83CHVDCZXR89JSSP69KAEW6","01M83CY39DE6FKT4TCXZ3K84RW","01M83FTJKF6TSA0B47EGG2WAS0","01M83FTNXGYJWFP0070QW585NT","01M83FTX3JP0DCZ1J4WM224T3S","01M83FV8899XACPZW7FQ80GS9G","01M83FVEB4T3PMP1Y6ZAKXQ0JY","01M83FVN3M0QEPEJZTBXKQ257P","01M83FW7RTFWGAVZ7VA2FS373P","01M83FWBTBP9MG0XG736WWAMJR","01M83FWGRGABHC2NKRFVK426W8","01M83FWSH47M7WD801TN70YFTT","01M83FX7SX9YW561N14X2ARVFX"]},"why":""}
